            "matched_surface": "skip-gram model",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_164aa8ee5320ab83fa370233",
            "source_text": "In natural language processing applications, the center word vectors of the skip-gram model are typically\nused as the word representations.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b012",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "b7eba23c9583e3c350dae8f267a2506258bfb50008c71fb71a4f891171b200ab",
            "context_id": "ctx_7ab8e2d37def67d0148f52d5",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP",
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "skip-gram model",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_9a96571ee9889acc457a68cf",
            "source_text": "As shown in :numref:`fig_skip_gram`,\ngiven the center word \"loves\",\nthe skip-gram model considers\nthe conditional probability for generating the *context words*: \"the\", \"man\", \"his\", and \"son\",\nwhich are no more than 2 words away from the center word:",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b019",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
            "content_sha256": "5221a9032bce0663211978d4b8bf1fafc01bdde58ac1e0538e58dda813538a19",
            "context_id": "ctx_9afa421e80e79b49583f6bb8",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP",
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "skip-gram model",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_cb5a6526da0bdc717a0af1b5",
            "source_text": "For context window size $m$,\nthe likelihood function of the skip-gram model\nis the probability of generating all context words\ngiven any center word:",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining_word2vec_b016",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_natural_language_processing_pretraining",
